# Mailslip: Git & commits

Single-repo app (`mailslip/`). Run git from the repo root.

## When to commit

- **Only commit when the user explicitly asks.** Never auto-commit.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, or build output (`.next/`, `node_modules/`).

## Commit shape

- Prefer **Conventional Commits:** `feat|fix|chore|docs|refactor|test|ci|build|perf`.
- Imperative subject, no trailing period. Keep the header ≤ 72 characters when practical.

## No AI attribution in git history

- No `Co-authored-by:` lines (`Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any agent).
- No `Made-with-Cursor`, `generated-by`, or similar footers.
- Use `git commit` with `-m` / HEREDOC only. **Never** pass `--trailer` or co-author flags.
- If a commit on disk includes agent co-author text **before push**, amend the message to remove it.
- After commit, run `git log -1 --format=%B` and confirm there is **no** `Co-authored-by` line before `git push`.

### When Cursor still injects a trailer

`git commit -m` may append `Co-authored-by` from IDE/CLI attribution. Amend with an editor that writes only your message:

```bash
cat > /tmp/mailslip-git-editor.sh << 'SCRIPT'
#!/bin/sh
printf '%s\n' "type: subject" > "$1"
SCRIPT
chmod +x /tmp/mailslip-git-editor.sh
GIT_EDITOR=/tmp/mailslip-git-editor.sh git commit --amend
```

Disable **Cursor Settings → Agent → Attribution**. CLI: `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` →
`attribution.attributeCommitsToAgent` / `attributePRsToAgent` = `false`.

## Pre-commit

Run applicable gates before commit when the change touches app code: `npm run lint`,
`npm run build` (or project scripts in `package.json`). Fix failures before committing.

## Safety

- Never force-push `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
